This derivative is independent of the original maintainers, KernelSU, TikTok
and device vendors. Source research, compilation, JVM/Node and browser mock
checks do not imply endorsement or compatibility with every Android device.
Compatibility is determined from available platform interfaces, not a device model.
The scoped Android16 AOSP review does not exhaust OEM native property paths.
The intended removal path is KernelSU removal plus a full phone reboot; it does
not delete an App's own cached responses, manager logs or user SIM renames.

Version 0.6.0 links a Rust data core and ships Rust-native upgrade executables.
The Kotlin Compose UI, Java Android interfaces/controller and C++ Zygisk/ART
bridge remain. Rust toolchain 1.100.0 is pinned to official 2026-11-12 components.
Rust standard library and its third-party notices are in Rust_std_COPYRIGHT.txt,
Rust_std_LICENSE-APACHE.txt and Rust_std_LICENSE-MIT.txt under native-licenses.
Linked Cargo crates include serde_json, serde_core, libc, memchr, itoa and zmij;
versions/checksums are pinned in rust-core/Cargo.lock, with license copies under
native-licenses/Rust_*. Rust FFI and native hooks still have unsafe boundaries.

